From b7020a82998f9d78058536f8df7e3f75ef9e8e6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 00:27:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ADR-0008: rebase ambient baseline to the ending reading at
 session end

Fixes a real gap surfaced by inspection (not yet an observed incident,
but demonstrated directly against real logged data): _baseline (the
ADR-0004 ambient EMA tracker) is frozen the entire time a session is
ACTIVE/COOLDOWN and only resumes updating once back in IDLE. Before
ADR-0006 this was harmless -- a session could only reach IDLE once
humidity had already decayed close to the frozen threshold, so the
stale baseline and current humidity were already close together.
ADR-0006 breaks that assumption: a session can now end via the
presence-corroborated path while humidity is still far above true
ambient (78%, 80% in the two incidents that motivated it).

The EMA's catch-up from that stale value depends on dt -- roughly how
long the just-ended session ran, not how long ago it ended, since the
baseline was frozen throughout. Replaying the real incident #1 data
shows this directly: baseline jumped from a stale 49.2 to 73.24 on the
first post-IDLE reading, landing close to correct mostly by chance of
that session having run ~20 minutes (large dt -> alpha near 1). A SHORT
first session (e.g. an early ADR-0006 false-start catch within a couple
of minutes) would produce a small dt and barely move the baseline at
all, leaving a second person's real shower measured against a
near-stale reference -- their modest actual rise could look like it
already exceeds max_humidity_delta, cutting water almost immediately.
The opposite failure (delayed STARTED detection) is also possible
depending on exactly where the partial catch-up lands.

This was concretely simulated: a synthetic "second shower right after
the first ends" scenario, appended to incident #1's real trace, was
replayed under both the old and new logic. Under the old logic the
second shower's delta baseline is contaminated by the original stale
49.2 ambient. Under the fix, it correctly reflects the accurate,
recently-tracked room condition, and the second shower's cut only fires
once ITS OWN humidity contribution genuinely exceeds max_humidity_delta
above where the room actually was -- not an inherited gap.

This mirrors and extends a guarantee the codebase already provides in a
narrower case: RESUMED already resets active_since_humidity to the raw
current reading (not the stale session-start baseline) specifically so
a sibling shower during the same session's COOLDOWN window gets its own
accurate baseline. This ADR extends that same accuracy guarantee across
the brief IDLE gap once a session has fully ended, since ADR-0006 means
that gap can now open while the room is still genuinely humid.

Fix: _end_session() now sets self._baseline = humidity and
self._baseline_updated_at = now, in addition to its existing
session-scoped state cleanup. Applies uniformly regardless of which
path ended the session (COOLDOWN's decline/timeout fallback, or
ACTIVE's ADR-0006 presence-corroborated path) since all funnel through
_end_session(). For a "normal" ending (humidity already near baseline),
this rebase is a near no-op -- it only changes behavior for the case
ADR-0006 specifically introduced.

No new config keys. _update_baseline()'s ordinary EMA is unchanged --
this only changes what it starts from.

- session.py: _end_session() rebases _baseline / _baseline_updated_at.
  Docstrings updated (module header, _update_baseline).
- const.py / __init__.py / manifest.json: version bump only (1.9.0).
- Tests: 3 new tests in test_session.py -- baseline snaps exactly to
  the ending reading; a deliberately short first session (the old
  logic's worst case) still gets an exact immediate correction
  regardless of elapsed time; and a regression test simulating a second
  shower starting shortly after the first ends at high humidity,
  confirming its own delta baseline is accurate rather than inherited.
  Full suite: 119 passed (116 previously passing + 3 new).
- README.md / BACKLOG.md updated.

See adr/ADR-0008-baseline-rebase-at-session-end.md for full rationale,
including alternatives considered (scoping the rebase to only the
ADR-0006 path; a shorter baseline_time_constant_seconds default
instead; extending RESUMED's own mechanism across the IDLE gap).
